@@ -0,0 +1,315 @@
+# K=16 Terminal Cone Gate Report (GPT-5.5)
+
+Date: 2026-09-03  
+Lane: `k16-cone-gate-gpt55-20260903`  
+Frozen inputs: `/tmp/jc2-lane.JyEMIr/inputs`  
+Driver/output directory: `box/k16conegate-20260903/`
+
+## Input Integrity
+
+The lane receipt `xmodel/k16-cone-gate-gpt55-20260903.run.v2` was used as the
+mechanical source for the hash manifest.  I generated the check file with
+`awk` from its `charged_input_<i>_sha256=` and `charged_input_<i>_basename=`
+lines, then ran `sha256sum -c`.  All 25 frozen inputs checked `OK`.  The first
+attempt tried to place the generated manifest under the read-only input
+directory and failed with a filesystem error; rerunning into writable `/tmp`
+produced the passing manifest.  This was not a content mismatch.
+
+No ledger files, `jc2-lean`, or the forbidden in-progress lane report files were
+edited.  All new drivers and outputs are under `box/k16conegate-20260903/`.
+
+## Method
+
+I used the charged Opus, Sol, spine, and Grok reports as mathematical sources,
+then replayed the following controls locally:
+
+- `symbolic_weight_audit.py`: symbolic weight-balance check of the Sol Section 2
+  coefficient recurrence.
+- `record_weight_audit.py`: finite weighted-homogeneity check on frozen terminal
+  records `t=2,3,4,5` and frozen `b4=0` chart records through `t=6`.
+- `b3_axis_replay.py`: symbolic derivation of the B3-axis formulas and frozen
+  record restriction checks.
+- `emit_singular_jobs.py` and `run_singular_jobs.py`: bounded Singular jobs for
+  `t=2` tau/Rabinowitsch controls and fixed-`t` homogeneous `std + dim` tests.
+
+Every Singular invocation had an explicit timeout.  The exact `t=5` homogeneous
+`std` job hit its 1200-second cap.  An exact `modStd` variant was terminated by
+the operator because it spawned more than two worker processes; it is recorded
+as `ABORTED_CORE_LIMIT` and is not mathematical evidence.  No
+`box/k16conegate-20260903` process remained running at seal time.
+
+## Lemma CONE
+
+Let
+
+```text
+A_t = Q[y]/(H_t),    H_t=12q^2y^2-12q(t+1)y+(t+1)(3t+2),    q=2t+1,
+d=2qy-(t+1),         so A_t = Q[d]/(3d^2-(t+1)).
+```
+
+A geometric point of `Spec A_t` means a morphism `Spec K -> Spec A_t`, where
+`K` is algebraically closed; equivalently, choose a root of `H_t` in `K`.  At
+split indices `t=3s^2-1`, the algebra over `Q` is `Q x Q`, with factors
+`d=+s` and `d=-s`, i.e.
+
+```text
+y=(t+1+s)/(2q),      y=(t+1-s)/(2q).
+```
+
+At `t=2`, these are `y=2/5` and `y=1/5`.  Statements over a split index must be
+checked factorwise; inverting a nonzero zero divisor in the product algebra is
+not allowed.
+
+On any geometric fibre, write
+
+```text
+I_{t,+}=<T_{t,1},...,T_{t,2t-1}>,      T_{t,0}=c+tau_t,
+```
+
+where `c` is the image of the banked unit and `tau_t` is homogeneous of weight
+`4t+1`.  Since the positive rows are homogeneous for weights
+
+```text
+wt(b4)=1, wt(q_{i,0})=i, wt(b3)=t+1,
+```
+
+`Z_+=V(I_{t,+})` is stable under
+`lambda.(b4,q_i,b3)=(lambda b4,lambda^i q_i,lambda^(t+1)b3)`.  If `tau_t`
+vanishes on `Z_+`, then `T_{t,0}=c` on `Z_+`, and `c != 0` on the fibre, so the
+full terminal zero set is empty.  Conversely, if some `x in Z_+` has
+`tau_t(x) != 0`, algebraic closedness gives `lambda^(4t+1)=-c/tau_t(x)`, hence
+`lambda.x in Z_+` and `T_{t,0}(lambda.x)=0`.  Nullstellensatz gives the
+fiberwise equivalence
+
+```text
+<I_{t,+},c+tau_t>=[1]  iff  tau_t in sqrt(I_{t,+}).
+```
+
+If `dim I_{t,+}=0` as a weighted-homogeneous ideal on the fibre, then the cone
+`Z_+` is only the origin: any nonzero point would carry a positive-dimensional
+`G_m` orbit.  Since `tau_t` has positive weight, `tau_t(0)=0`, so `dim=0`
+suffices for (8.1).
+
+Verdict: **CONFIRMED**, fibrewise for every integer `t>=2`, with the split-index
+qualification above.
+
+## Spine Grading (2.1)
+
+The charged grading is
+
+```text
+wt(h)=wt(s)=wt(b4)=1,
+wt(C_j)=j       (1<=j<=t-1),
+wt(q_{j,0})=j   (2<=j<=2t),
+wt(T(0))=t,
+wt(b_i)=(4-i)t+1, so wt(b1,b2,b3,b4)=(3t+1,2t+1,t+1,1),
+wt(y)=wt(g)=wt(g1)=wt(g2)=wt(c)=0.
+```
+
+The symbolic audit checks the coefficient recurrence, not just fixed records.
+It verifies
+
+```text
+wt(U_m)=q-m,         wt(C_m)=t-1-m,
+wt(B_m)=t-m,         wt(S_m)=2t-m,
+wt(V_m)=t+1-m,       wt(Y_m)=2t+1-m,       wt(Z_m)=t+1-m,
+wt(P0'_m)=3t-m,      wt(R_m)=4t+1-m.
+```
+
+After the change back from `L=X-b4` to `X`, the factor `b4^(m-k)` gives
+`wt(T_{t,k})=4t+1-k` for `k>0`; `T_{t,0}` has the same weight-`4t+1`
+nonconstant part plus the scalar `c`.  The audit output is
+`SYMBOLIC_WEIGHT_AUDIT = PASS`.
+
+The finite record audit also passed on all frozen records available for this
+lane:
+
+```text
+terminal_laurent_t2,t3,t4,t5: terminal rows and pivot RHS homogeneous;
+chart_t3_b4_0, chart_t5_b4_0, chart_t6_b4_0: same after b4=0 specialization.
+```
+
+This covers fixed records for `t=2..6` in the frozen input block.  The `b4=1`
+chart records are dehomogenized, so they are not a homogeneity test.
+
+Verdict: **CONFIRMED**, as an indexed consequence of the Sol recurrence and by
+finite record controls through the frozen `t=6` chart.
+
+## Proposition SUBCHART
+
+Let `R` be a subset of the residual variables
+`{b4,q_{2,0},...,q_{t-1,0},b3}` and let `S` set the complement to zero.  In the
+affine solve each eliminated variable `z_w` has the form
+
+```text
+z_w = -rho_w / p_w,
+```
+
+where `p_w` is a weight-zero unit of `A_t` and `rho_w` is homogeneous of weight
+`w` in the residual variables, after earlier substitutions by homogeneous
+solved values.  On `S`, every monomial involving a killed residual variable
+vanishes.  What remains is the span of monomials in `R` whose weights sum to
+`w`.  Therefore `z_w|_S=0` if `w` is outside the numerical semigroup generated
+by the surviving weights; if there is a unique monomial of weight `w`, the
+restriction is a single `A_t` scalar times that monomial.
+
+This is a grading plus affine-elimination statement.  It does not by itself
+assert radical membership in the original multivariable ideal.
+
+Verdict: **CONFIRMED**, with scope limited to coordinate subcharts after the
+weighted affine solve.
+
+## Theorem B3-AXIS
+
+Take
+
+```text
+S={b4=0, q_{2,0}=...=q_{t-1,0}=0}.
+```
+
+Then `Sem({b3})=(t+1)Z_{\ge 0}`.  In the high weights `1..2t+1`, the only
+surviving high variable is `q_{t+1,0}=lambda b3`; `T(0)`, `b1`, and `b2` have
+weights not divisible by `t+1` for `t>=2` and vanish on this subchart.  The
+symbolic replay solves the single remaining equation:
+
+```text
+lambda = -(6dt-3d+9t^2+2t-1)/(6t(3t-1)).
+```
+
+The restrictions are
+
+```text
+T_{t,2t-1}|_S = alpha_t b3^2,
+alpha_t = t(3t+1)((27t^3-30t^2+t-2)d + (6t^3+13t^2-3t+2))
+          /(12(2t+1)^2(3t-1)^2(3t+2)),
+
+T_{t,t-2}|_S = phi_t b3^3,
+phi_t = -t(t-2)(3t+1)(6td-(t+1))/(72(2t+1)^3(3t-1)),
+
+T_{t,k}|_S=0 for k not in {0,t-2,2t-1}, and T_{t,0}|_S=c
+```
+
+with the `t=2` overlap `t-2=0` interpreted as the band-zero row.  The replay
+computes the unit norms
+
+```text
+N(6td-(t+1)) = -(t+1)(3t-1)(4t+1),
+N(alpha linear part) =
+  -(t-2)(3t-1)^2(3t+2)(27t^3+17t^2+t+2)/3.
+```
+
+The first has no integer root `t>=1`; the second has the single positive
+integer root `t=2`.  The rational prefactor of `phi_t` also contains exactly
+the positive integer factor `t-2`.  Denominators have no positive integer
+roots in scope.  Hence `alpha_t` and `phi_t` are units in `A_t` for every
+`t>=3`.
+
+The frozen-record restriction check matched the formula on
+`terminal_laurent_t2,t3,t4,t5` and `chart_t3_b4_0, chart_t5_b4_0,
+chart_t6_b4_0`; output: `B3_AXIS_REPLAY = PASS`.
+
+Verdict: **CONFIRMED** for the stated axis restriction and unitness for
+`t>=3`; the `t=2` anomaly is exactly the numerator factor `t-2` plus the
+`alpha_t` norm factor.
+
+## t=2 Fibre
+
+The exact `t=2` replay gives
+
+```text
+T_{2,3}|_{b4=0} = 28 b3^2(5y-1)/625,
+tau_2 = b4^3 * (...),
+tau_2|_{b4=0}=0.
+```
+
+Thus on `y=1/5` the positive-band cone contains the whole `b3` axis on the
+`b4=0` fibre, while on `y=2/5` band 3 cuts it by a unit times `b3^2`.
+
+Bounded Singular results:
+
+```text
+t=2, y=1/5: dim(I_{2,+})=1, size=3;
+             Rabinowitsch tau in radical = 1; full ideal (8.1) unit = 1.
+t=2, y=2/5: dim(I_{2,+})=0, size=4;
+             Rabinowitsch tau in radical = 1; full ideal (8.1) unit = 1.
+```
+
+Therefore `RESIDUAL-ZERO` is false at `t=2` on the fibre `y=1/5`, but (8.1)
+holds there by Lemma CONE.  This is a direct counterexample to any all-`t>=2`
+version of `RESIDUAL-ZERO`.
+
+Verdict: **REFUTED** for all-`t>=2` `RESIDUAL-ZERO`; **CONFIRMED** for (8.1) on
+both `t=2` fibres.
+
+## Fixed-t Cone Tests
+
+The requested homogeneous `std + dim` tests for `I_{t,+}` produced:
+
+```text
+t=2, y=1/5: DIM=1, SIZE=3      negative control;
+t=2, y=2/5: DIM=0, SIZE=4;
+t=3:        DIM=0, SIZE=20     exact over Q[y]/(H_3);
+t=4:        DIM=0, SIZE=81     exact over Q[y]/(H_4);
+t=5:        exact std hit 1200s timeout, no dim verdict;
+t=5 mod 1009: DIM=0, SIZE=340  modular control only, not promoted.
+```
+
+Consequences: `dim=0` certifies (8.1) at `t=3` and `t=4` by Lemma CONE, and
+certifies the `y=2/5` fibre at `t=2`.  The `y=1/5` fibre at `t=2` is certified
+instead by the tau criterion.  The exact homogeneous dim route does **not**
+certify `t=5` in this lane.  The charged Sol report contains a separate exact
+two-chart `t=5` proof, but that is not the same as an exact homogeneous dim
+certificate.
+
+Verdict: **CONFIRMED** for `t=3,4`; **GAP/INCONCLUSIVE_TIMEOUT** for exact
+homogeneous dim at `t=5`; modular `t=5` is supporting evidence only.
+
+## Reduction of (8.1) to (10.1)
+
+The B3-axis theorem kills the `b3` direction on the `b4=0` cone for `t>=3`.
+The proposed (10.1),
+
+```text
+q_{j,0} in sqrt(I_{t,+}+(b4)) for 2<=j<=t-1,
+```
+
+would complete the remaining `q` directions of the `b4=0` cone.  Together with
+the unit constant in band zero, that would prove the `b4=0` chart.
+
+It does **not** complete (8.1) by itself.  Lemma CONE requires `tau_t` to vanish
+on the whole positive cone, not only on its `b4=0` slice.  Equivalently, a
+complete proof still needs a separate statement controlling the `b4 != 0`
+direction, such as `TOP-TAIL-UNIT` on `b4=1`, a proof that no positive-cone
+component survives with `b4` invertible, or a direct full-cone
+Rabinowitsch/dim argument.  Therefore the reduction of (8.1) to only (10.1) is
+incomplete.
+
+Verdict: **GAP** for the claimed reduction to just (10.1); a `b4` direction or
+`b4=1` chart statement remains necessary.
+
+## FALLACY-v2 Check
+
+No `sat()` wrapper was used.  Radical membership at `t=2` used the declared
+Rabinowitsch ideal `<I_{2,+},1-z tau_2>`.  Split indices were treated
+factorwise; the `t=2` product algebra was never used as a field.  Modular
+`t=5` was not promoted to characteristic zero.  Axis statements were not
+promoted to full multivariable radical containments.  Lower bounds and finite
+records were not converted into all-`t` induction claims.
